Package: DiffiScape
Title: Differentiable Landscape Connectivity Optimization
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Sean", "Sorek", , "sssorek1@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Fits landscape resistance and animal occurrence intensity from
    environmental rasters and location data using differentiable circuit
    connectivity. The independently installed 'diffiscape' Python package
    provides JAX-based connectivity, gradient and Gaussian-process surrogate
    optimization, built-in intensity likelihoods, and NumPyro posterior
    inference. The R interface handles spatial inputs, raster outputs, and
    plotting. The derivative-free workflow also supports 'mgcv' generalized
    additive models and custom R callbacks.
